  "methods": [
    "Every source_trace joins connected source ports and named source nets in an independently constructed DSU.",
    "SMT rectangles/polygons/circles, rotated pill/circle PTH lands, all-through barrels, maximum-adjacent-width swept trace segments and exact native BREP pours are checked on every occupied layer.",
    "Layer-specific drilled voids are subtracted from every conductor before overlap measurement; polygon circle approximation uses 1024 edges. Analytic trace/trace, via/via and via/trace centerline gap calculations preserve continuous round copper extents.",
    "STRtree dwithin=.251 mm searches every native copper pair. Net identity exemptions depend on source graph roots, never matching labels, accepted pass flags or expected rendered appearance.",
    "All-through barrels; circle/circle gaps analytic; native rotated pill slot void distances use 1024-edge round geometry. Every pair is checked, including same-net barrels.",
    "Maximum-width native trace sweeps clipped to the actual crop window. Net roots come from a freshly hash-verified source ownership map; candidates follow source names rather than stale Source23 PCB IDs. Copper union area describes trace sweeps only, not via lands or the drill Boolean model, which are covered by the separate whole-board native audit."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Ideal native CAD geometry only; soldermask, etch/drill tolerances and bench continuity are outside this short check.",
    "Unknown copper objects are reported and retain unique foreign roots, so isolated fiducials do not silently share a net.",
    "No declared trace/trace, pour/trace, pour/pad or pour/pour clearance field exists; their .20 mm proximity screening is explicitly distinguished from board policy.",
    "This role does not establish whole-net continuity, route efficiency, soldermask/silkscreen readiness, electrical dynamic behavior or bench performance. Gerber manufacturing geometry is checked separately by root."
  ],
